                <pb facs="0168" n="118" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg118"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Jernigan to Mr.
                            Uhl.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">U.
                                S. Consulate-General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1894-10-09"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October 9, 1894</hi></date>. (Received
                        November 13.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: * * * The two alleged Japanese spies are
                    alive, and have all they need to eat and drink. Many of the reports in the home
                    papers about them are so false as to be past finding out.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. R. Jernigan.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
